🌐 Elastic Load Balancer (ELB) – Complete Deep Notes
🧩 1. What is Elastic Load Balancer (ELB)?

ELB (Elastic Load Balancer) automatically distributes incoming traffic across multiple EC2 instances, containers, or IPs within one or more Availability Zones.

It ensures:

High availability

Fault tolerance

Scalability

Health monitoring

Think of it as a traffic manager for your AWS servers.

💡 Example

Imagine you have 3 EC2 web servers behind one load balancer.
When users access your website, the ELB automatically divides requests among all healthy servers.

🧱 2. Types of Load Balancers in AWS
Load Balancer	Layer	Use Case	Protocols	Example
Classic Load Balancer (CLB)	Layer 4 & 7	Legacy applications	HTTP, HTTPS, TCP	Old web servers
Application Load Balancer (ALB)	Layer 7	Modern web apps (routing, microservices)	HTTP, HTTPS	Web apps, APIs
Network Load Balancer (NLB)	Layer 4	High-performance, low-latency apps	TCP, UDP	Gaming, real-time apps
Gateway Load Balancer (GLB)	Layer 3	Security appliances (firewall, IPS)	IP	Firewalls, proxy
⚙️ 3. Classic Load Balancer (CLB)
📘 Overview

Operates at Layer 4 & Layer 7.

Distributes traffic evenly between EC2 instances.

Checks instance health using health checks.

Older model, being replaced by ALB/NLB.

🪜 Steps: Create Classic Load Balancer

Go to EC2 → Load Balancers → Create Load Balancer

Choose Classic Load Balancer

Configure:

Name: my-clb

Listener: HTTP (port 80)

Add at least 2 EC2 instances under the same VPC/subnet.

Configure Health Check path (/index.html)

Review → Create

⚙️ Access via Load Balancer

Once created, note the DNS name:

my-clb-123456789.ap-south-1.elb.amazonaws.com


Access in browser — it routes traffic to all healthy EC2s.

💡 Health Checks

CLB continuously checks the health of instances.
If an instance fails health checks, ELB stops routing traffic to it.

🔁 4. Access EC2 via Load Balancer Only

You can restrict direct access to instances:

Security Group (SG) of EC2: allow traffic only from Load Balancer’s SG.

Users connect via ELB DNS → ELB forwards to EC2.

✅ Improves security and hides EC2 public IP.

🗑 5. Delete Classic Load Balancer

Go to EC2 → Load Balancers → Select → Delete

Ensure DNS name is no longer active.

🧠 6. Application Load Balancer (ALB)
📘 Overview

Operates at Layer 7 (HTTP/HTTPS).

Smart routing: can route based on path, host, headers, or query string.

Supports microservices, containers, and ECS/EKS.

🧩 ALB Architecture
Client → ALB → Target Group → EC2 Instances


Listeners: define incoming protocol/port (e.g., HTTP:80)

Target Groups: group of EC2s or containers

Rules: route based on URL path or hostname

🪜 Steps: Create ALB

Go to EC2 → Load Balancers → Create Load Balancer

Select Application Load Balancer

Configure:

Name: my-alb

Scheme: internet-facing

Listeners: HTTP (80)

Add subnets from 2 AZs for high availability.

Create Target Group:

Type: Instances

Protocol: HTTP (80)

Health check path: /

Register EC2s in Target Group.

Create ALB.

🧭 7. Path-Based Routing (ALB Feature)

You can route based on URL path:

URL Path	Target Group
/app1/*	App1 servers
/app2/*	App2 servers

Example Rule:

IF path is /api/* → forward to API Target Group.

🌍 8. Host-Based Routing (ALB Feature)

Route traffic based on domain name.

Domain	Target Group
app1.example.com	App1 EC2s
app2.example.com	App2 EC2s

This is commonly used in multi-domain applications.

🔄 9. Stickiness (Session Affinity)

Ensures user requests always go to the same backend EC2.

Useful for login sessions or shopping carts.

Enable in Target Group settings:

Type: Application-based cookie or Duration-based cookie.

🕵️ 10. Get Client IP in Application Server

When traffic goes through ALB, the real client IP is hidden.
To capture the client IP:

Check the X-Forwarded-For header in your web server logs.

Example (Nginx):

log_format main '$remote_addr forwarded_for=$http_x_forwarded_for';

⚡ 11. Network Load Balancer (NLB)
📘 Overview

Operates at Layer 4 (TCP/UDP).

Designed for millions of requests per second.

Very low latency, static IP support.

💡 Use Cases

Financial applications

Gaming servers

Real-time data streaming

🪜 Steps: Create NLB

Go to Load Balancers → Create → Network Load Balancer

Name: my-nlb

Scheme: internet-facing

Listeners: TCP 80 or 443

Add subnets → 2 AZs

Create Target Group (TCP)

Register instances

Create.

💡 NLB provides 1 static IP per AZ — great for whitelisting firewalls.

🔁 12. Auto Scaling Integration with ELB

Combine ELB + Auto Scaling Group (ASG) for fault tolerance:

ELB distributes traffic.

ASG automatically launches/replaces unhealthy EC2s.

✅ Traffic distribution + instance lifecycle automation.

🔒 13. Security Groups for ELB
Resource	Inbound	Outbound
Load Balancer	Allow 80/443 (public)	To Target Group
EC2 Instances	Allow from ELB SG	Outbound to anywhere
🧾 14. ELB Monitoring (Metrics)
Metric	Description
RequestCount	Number of requests handled
HealthyHostCount	Healthy targets
UnHealthyHostCount	Failed targets
TargetResponseTime	Average response time
HTTPCode_Target_5XX	Backend errors

Use CloudWatch for alerts.

🧹 15. Delete ALB or NLB

Go to Load Balancers → Select → Delete.

Delete associated Target Groups to avoid charges.

🧠 16. Interview Questions – Elastic Load Balancer
❓ Question	💡 Answer
What is ELB?	Distributes traffic across multiple EC2 instances for high availability.
Types of Load Balancers?	CLB, ALB, NLB, Gateway LB.
Difference between ALB and NLB?	ALB = HTTP (Layer 7); NLB = TCP (Layer 4).
What is Path-based Routing?	Routes traffic based on URL path like /api/.
What is Host-based Routing?	Routes based on hostname like api.example.com.
What is Stickiness?	Keeps user sessions on the same backend EC2.
How to find client IP behind ALB?	Using X-Forwarded-For header.
What’s the use of Target Group?	Logical group of instances where ALB sends traffic.
Can we attach ELB to multiple AZs?	Yes, at least two for HA.
Difference between Classic and Application LB?	CLB = basic, ALB = smart routing & microservices.
What is the listener in ALB?	A process that checks for incoming connections (port/protocol).
Does NLB support static IPs?	Yes, one per AZ.
Can ALB handle WebSocket or HTTP/2?	Yes, fully supported.
How ELB detects unhealthy instances?	Health checks (HTTP, TCP, HTTPS).
What is Cross-Zone Load Balancing?	Evenly distributes traffic across AZs.
